From 45aba360c0e1c43e32160efe832a1d63ab1bcb41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:25:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OrionLayer Open Fix 36: send where the colony screen puts its
 buildings ("CBLD")

While SCREEN_COLONY is up, the snapshot ends (after COLS) in a "CBLD"
block: the 36 int16 building ids of COLONY::_colony_bldgs, row by row,
then the ten int16 COLONY::_colony_satellites.

Why: Make_Bldg_Array_For_Colony_ (colony_main.cpp:536-631) places the
buildings with game_random seeded by the colony index plus Random_ draws,
and the scene and the roads follow those arrays. Which buildings a colony
has is on the wire, where they stand is not, and a client copy would have
to transcribe the RNG. OrionLayer does not place buildings from it yet
(UNVERIFIED building_placement: the grid also holds housing and jittered
satellites).

OrionLayer, open fix 36 (orionlayerv3 doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md,
doc/ext_colony_building_placement.patch). Approved by Data (brief 180,
item 1); applied by work order 181. Local only, never pushed.

Ported onto orion2re v2.0.0 in scratch (work order 242 e) from local 01bafd9c:
renamed 3-way merge (identifier map cf4d9617->v2.0.0), clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ext/ext_api.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 760630e6..fda4af0f 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -468,6 +468,31 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         Write8(buf, COLONY::field_mode);
         Write8(buf, BUILD_QUEUE::autobuild_settings.enabled);
     }
+
+    // 7. Where the colony screen puts its buildings: "CBLD", written ONLY
+    //    while SCREEN_COLONY is up, and LAST. OrionLayer, open fix 36.
+    //
+    //    Make_Bldg_Array_For_Colony (colony_main.cpp:536-631) places the
+    //    colony's buildings on a 6x6 grid and its satellites in ten slots
+    //    with game_random seeded by the colony index plus Random_ draws;
+    //    Draw_Colony_Bldgs and Draw_Colony_Satellites draw from those two
+    //    arrays. A client would have to transcribe the RNG exactly, so the
+    //    arrays are sent as they are: 36 building ids, row by row, then the
+    //    ten satellite ids. Valid while COLS's handle agrees with its pair.
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_COLONY) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'C');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'B');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'L');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'D');
+        for (int r = 0; r < 6; r++) {
+            for (int c = 0; c < 6; c++) {
+                Write16(buf, (int16_t)COLONY::colony_bldgs[r].buildings[c]);
+            }
+        }
+        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
+            Write16(buf, COLONY::colony_satellites[i]);
+        }
+    }
 }
 
